## Verified resolved

1. **`newline-lines` (P2 bug)** — `lower.cljc:222-239`. Code-checked, not taken from the claim: one `inc` iff a `NEWLINE` token's text contains `\n`, `\r` or `\f`. CRLF (`"\r\n"`) is one token containing both and advances **1**; alone `"\r"` advances 1; `"\f"` advances 1; the start-of-input `SPACES` alternative contains none of the three and advances **0**. The grammar's second alternative admits exactly one break sequence (`'\r'? '\n' | '\r' | '\f'`), so "one per token" is exactly "the line breaks", matching `yang.antlr.md:1714`. `manifest.edn` confirms the patched lexer base pins NEWLINE's span to the newline characters, so the token text really is `"\r\n"` / `"\f"`. The docstring now states the rule correctly.
